1.1 Lineage
===========

   • Lean4-Mode (https://github.com/leanprover-community/lean4-mode) is
     the Lean community's Emacs mode for Lean 4.
   • Nael is Mekeor Melire's fork of it, on Codeberg
     (https://codeberg.org/mekeor/nael) and Melpa
     (https://melpa.org/#/nael).  Lena's major mode, its Font-Lock
     rules, navigation and much of this manual are Nael's.  Lena's input
     method starts from Mekeor Melire's work on Nael's ‘dev’ branch.
   • Lena branched from Nael 0.8.3 (commit ‘c1d3497’ of Nael's ‘release’
     branch) and was later renamed to Lena.
   • It builds on code from elsewhere: ‘lena-eglot.el’'s building of
     imports (‘dependencyBuildMode’) and restarting of files are adapted
     from Doug Torrance's lean4-mode
     (https://github.com/d-torrance/lean4-mode); ‘lena-rpc.el’ is
     derived from that lean4-mode's ‘lean4-rpc.el’, which is derived
     from Jan Mas Rovira's neo-lean-mode
     (https://github.com/janmasrovira/neo-lean-mode); the smartparens
     pairs and the Doom Emacs setup in this manual follow Doom Emacs'
     own ‘:lang lean’ module.  See _License and Maintenance_ and
     ‘NOTICE’.


